{
  "abstract": "We construct an explicit two-parameter family of smooth projective surfaces with geometric genus four and irregularity one, and prove the rational Hodge conjecture in every codimension on every power of one very general fibre. The surfaces arise as adjacent-reflection quotients in a dihedral double tower built from the known genus-29 quaternionic Prym family. We determine the actual invariant field and central branch, show that the reverse norm surface is elliptic ruled, and give a genus-two Albanese fibration with its nonconstant quadratic twist retained. The dihedral graph-trace correspondence has transpose-composition two on the full inherited odd cohomology, giving algebraic cohomological retractions to the previously studied quaternionic eightfold and an elliptic curve. A separate independence argument is essential for their mixed products. At a boundary collision, anticommuting involutions make four half-twists act identically on the Prym's parabolic cochains, while the elliptic curve has nontrivial unipotent monodromy. Normality and the simplicity of $\\mathfrak{sl}_2$ imply product generic Hodge group. Existing determinant cycles on the eightfold, elliptic invariant theory and the retractions then prove the surface theorem. A standalone supplement verifies the finite groups, exact field identities, genus-two factorization, local braid identity and elliptic isogeny. The result concerns self-powers of a very general fibre; special-fibre classes and the general Hodge conjecture remain outside its scope.",
